<title>CANADA: Canada's Martin says government on track fiscally.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin says government on track fiscally.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin, faced with calls within his Liberal Party for more spending, said on Wednesday the newly re-elected government was on course in its battle against the deficit.</p>
<p>Asked by Reuters if he planned to continue with the pace of deficit cutting, he said only: &quot;We're on track with the deficit. We're on track.&quot;</p>
<p>Martin has hardly said a word to the media since the June 2 election. He was reappointed to his post during a general cabinet shuffle on Wednesday.</p>
<p>((Reuters Ottawa Bureau 613-235-6745))</p>
</text>
